From 80b8089282a4314ff3c70eb5c70603fc75719bce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sn3ro <zak.darek@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 06:37:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(recognize): read a slot with holes through or tangent to
 its floor

detect_pockets returned nothing for the p01-flange slot. Two through
holes in its floor are tangent to the slot wall, so the floor's rings
share a vertex, and the feature walk reported every ring as open. With
the holes off the wall, any inner ring still refused the slot.

- slot_of refuses a boss only: an inner ring whose edge facets stand
  above the floor. A hole through the floor keeps the slot.
- recognize::pinch takes the walk's knotted rings as the outer ring and
  its holes only when it proves them: simple rings of face boundary
  edges, holes inside the largest ring, and the area identity with the
  face's facet area. Anything else stays refused.

Pinned by a_slot_with_a_hole_tangent_to_its_wall_is_still_a_slot,
a_slot_with_holes_through_its_floor_is_still_a_slot and
a_boss_standing_in_the_channel_is_not_a_slot (mcp_pockets).

Fixes #2440

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
